---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DelayCalculator from '../components/DelayCalculator.astro';
import TapPad from '../components/TapPad.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Delay Pedal with Tap Tempo & Reverb Time Calculator (ms) | ttaptempo.com"
  description="Calculate exact milliseconds (ms) and Hertz for your delay pedal with tap tempo and studio DAW plugins. Sync 1/4, 1/8 dotted, and triplet echoes with 1-click copy."
  keywords="delay pedal with tap tempo, delay time calculator, reverb pre-delay calculator, bpm to ms, tap tempo delay, bpm delay chart"
  canonicalPath="/delay-calculator/"
>
  <div class="py-6 px-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-2">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>Delay &amp; Reverb Calculator</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <DelayCalculator />
  <TapPad />

  <!-- Dedicated Delay Pedal Guide -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
    <article class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-sm sm:text-base">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-4">
        How to Sync a Delay Pedal with Tap Tempo
      </h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>delay pedal with tap tempo</strong> is one of the most expressive tools in a guitarist or synthesizer player's arsenal. By setting the delay repeat intervals in exact mathematical synchronization with the song tempo, you achieve lush, musical ambiance without frequency muddiness.
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mt-6 mb-3">
        Popular Delay Rhythm Divisions
      </h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Dotted Eighth Note (1/8d):</strong> The classic edge delay rhythm used in arena rock and ambient worship music. Creates a driving gallop feel against straight eighth notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Quarter Note (1/4):</strong> Standard rhythmic repeat sitting directly in pocket behind your chords and melodies.</li>
        <li><strong>Triplet Delays (1/8t):</strong> Perfect for blues shuffle, reggae dub, and 6/8 ballads.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
